# Varys — Jenkins CI Intelligence Agent
## Master Implementation Blueprint & Architecture Guide

> **"A spider has many little whisperers."**  
> Varys is an autonomous, multi-turn AI diagnostic agent that investigates Jenkins CI pipeline failures, flakiness, and performance regressions by reasoning across build history, test execution patterns, and code commit diffs.

---

## 1. Executive Summary

| Attribute | Specification |
|---|---|
| **Project Name** | `varys` |
| **Type** | CLI Diagnostic Tool & Agent Loop |
| **Primary Interface** | `$ varys "why is the payment-pipeline job unstable?"` |
| **Reasoning Model** | Autonomous multi-turn ReAct tool loop (max 5 iterations) |
| **Core Protocol** | Model Context Protocol (MCP) Server |
| **Target Execution Time** | < 10 seconds per investigation |
| **Scope Boundary** | **Read & Diagnose Only** (No CI write actions / test quarantines) |

---

## 2. System Architecture

```
                      ┌────────────────────────────────────────┐
                      │             User / CLI                 │
                      │  $ varys "why is payment-pipeline red?"│
                      └──────────────────┬─────────────────────┘
                                         │
                                         ▼
                      ┌────────────────────────────────────────┐
                      │         Varys Agent Orchestrator       │
                      │  - Plan & Goal decomposition           │
                      │  - Multi-step ReAct Loop (max 5 turns) │
                      │  - Context window & trace management   │
                      └──────────────────┬─────────────────────┘
                                         │ Tool Calling Protocol
                                         ▼
                      ┌────────────────────────────────────────┐
                      │          Varys MCP Tool Server         │
                      │                                        │
                      │  [1] get_recent_builds(job, count)     │
                      │  [2] get_test_results(job, build_num)  │
                      │  [3] get_test_history(job, test, count)│
                      │  [4] get_commits_between(b_a, b_b)     │
                      └──────────────────┬─────────────────────┘
                                         │
                     ┌───────────────────┴───────────────────┐
                     ▼                                       ▼
        ┌─────────────────────────┐             ┌─────────────────────────┐
        │   SQLite / JSON Store   │             │   Live Jenkins API      │
        │  (Seeded Scenario DB)   │             │   (Optional Adapter)    │
        │ - Scenario A: Flaky+Cfg │             │                         │
        │ - Scenario B: Slow Regr │             │                         │
        └─────────────────────────┘             └─────────────────────────┘
```

---

## 3. Phased Implementation Roadmap

The implementation is broken down into 6 discrete, testable phases:

| Phase | Title | Focus Area | Deliverables | Target Timeline |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **[Phase 1](./phases/01_data_and_scenarios.md)** | **Data & Seed Scenarios** | Deterministic test beds | SQLite schema, JSON fixtures, Seed generator for Scenario A (Flaky+Config) & B (Duration Regression) | Days 1–2 |
| **[Phase 2](./phases/02_mcp_server_and_tools.md)** | **MCP Server & Tool Contracts** | Data access layer | FastMCP / standard MCP server with 4 core tool endpoints & unit test suite | Days 3–4 |
| **[Phase 3](./phases/03_agent_loop_orchestration.md)** | **Agent Loop & Reasoning Engine** | Multi-turn ReAct loop | Dynamic tool calling engine, prompt templates, loop safeguards (turn caps, error fallbacks) | Days 5–7 |
| **[Phase 4](./phases/04_heuristics_and_diagnostics.md)** | **Heuristics & Correlation Layer** | Analytical depth | Flakiness score heuristic, Duration regression detector, Commit attribution mapper | Days 8–10 |
| **[Phase 5](./phases/05_cli_and_ux.md)** | **CLI & Live Trace UI** | User Experience | Terminal streaming UI, step-by-step investigation trace spinner, formatted diagnosis cards | Days 11–12 |
| **[Phase 6](./phases/06_verification_and_demo.md)** | **End-to-End Testing & Interview Guide** | Quality & Defense | Automated verification suite, demo scripts, FAQ & interview defense cheatsheet | Days 13–14 |

---

