├── varys/
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── cli.py                           # CLI entrypoint ($ varys "...")
│   ├── agent/                           # Agent loop & prompt orchestration
│   │   ├── __init__.py
│   │   ├── loop.py                      # ReAct orchestrator loop
│   │   ├── prompts.py                   # System & analysis prompts
│   │   └── types.py                     # AgentState, StepResult, Diagnosis
│   ├── mcp/                             # MCP Server and tool definitions
│   │   ├── __init__.py
│   │   ├── server.py                    # MCP server definition
│   │   └── tools.py                     # Tool functions & contracts
│   ├── heuristics/                      # Analysis & correlation algorithms
│   │   ├── __init__.py
│   │   ├── flakiness.py                 # Pass/fail alternation & entropy
│   │   ├── regressions.py               # Duration trend change-point detection
│   │   └── commit_correlator.py         # Git file change to test mapping
│   ├── storage/                         # Database & mock scenario manager
│   │   ├── __init__.py
│   │   ├── database.py                  # SQLite DAO
│   │   └── seed.py                      # Deterministic scenario generator
│   └── ui/                              # Rich terminal UI components
│       ├── __init__.py
│       ├── console.py                   # Live spinner, step logger
│       └── renderer.py                  # Diagnosis card & diff renderer
└── tests/                               # Comprehensive test suite
    ├── test_scenarios.py
    ├── test_mcp_tools.py
    ├── test_agent_loop.py
    └── test_heuristics.py
```

---

## 5. Technology Stack Selection

- **Runtime & Language**: Python 3.11+
- **Agent Tool Protocol**: Model Context Protocol (MCP) via `mcp` / `FastMCP`
- **LLM Client**: `google-genai` / `anthropic` / `openai` / `litellm` (abstracted driver)
- **Local Storage**: `sqlite3` + `pydantic` (zero-overhead, deterministic, file-backed)
- **CLI & Formatting**: `typer` + `rich` (vibrant live spinners, syntax-highlighted diffs, clean tables)
- **Testing**: `pytest` + `pytest-asyncio`
